# Response headers for hosts that read this file — Cloudflare Pages and Netlify
# use this convention. GITHUB PAGES DOES NOT: it has no mechanism for custom
# response headers, and serves this file as a plain static asset at /_headers.
#
# So on Pages, none of the below is sent. What still applies there is the
# <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"> and <meta name="referrer"> in
# src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro, which browsers do honour. Keep the CSP here and
# the CSP there in sync.
#
# What is unavoidably lost on Pages: nosniff, Permissions-Policy, and
# frame-ancestors — the last because it is invalid in a meta tag, so nothing
# stops the site being framed. See the note in BaseLayout.astro.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
